10
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Just Friends is a 2005 Christmas romantic black comedy film directed by Roger Kumble, written by Adam 'Tex'
Davis and starring Ryan Reynolds, Amy Smart, Anna Faris, Chris Klein and Christopher Marquette.

11
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:48,000
The plot focuses on a formerly obese high school student (Reynolds) who attempts to free himself from the friend zone after
reconnecting with his best friend (Smart), with whom he is in love while visiting his hometown for Christmas.

12
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
The film revolves around humorous observation of strictly platonic
relationships as "just friends" or "just as best friends".

13
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:12,000
Davis's screenplay for Just Friends was initially optioned in 2001 by New Line
Cinema, and was inspired by numerous elements of his own life.

14
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:54,000
Principal photography took place in early 2005 in Los Angeles as
well as Regina and Moose Jaw, Saskatchewan, Canada.

15
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
The film was an international co-production between
the United States, Canada, and Germany.

16
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
Just Friends was released on November 23, 2005, and grossed over $50 million.

17
01:19:54,000 --> 01:20:00,000
It received mixed reviews from film critics, but has developed a
cult following in the years since its release.

18
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
The film explores themes of change, holiday, success, falling in love, hometown.

19
01:29:18,000 --> 01:29:24,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
